  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a skillet over medium heat, melt butter. Let the butter cook until it's slightly browned. Add curry leaves. Stir and cook until aromatic.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/ground-beef-and-butter-with-fresh-curry-leaves/#wprm-recipe-53349-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/ground-beef-butter-curry-leaves-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add ground beef. Break up and cook until no longer pink. Generously season with salt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/ground-beef-and-butter-with-fresh-curry-leaves/#wprm-recipe-53349-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/ground-beef-butter-curry-leaves-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add 1 inch of water to a pot, cover, and bring to a boil over high heat. Once boiling, add the eggs straight from the refrigerator into the pot. Replace the lid and let it continue to boil for about six minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/ground-beef-and-butter-with-fresh-curry-leaves/#wprm-recipe-53349-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Once done, place the eggs in ice water or run under cold water until they are cool to the touch. Peel and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/ground-beef-and-butter-with-fresh-curry-leaves/#wprm-recipe-53349-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer to serving or individual bowls. Sprinkle a pinch of crushed red pepper flakes for some kick. Serve with softboiled eggs and cheese.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/ground-beef-and-butter-with-fresh-curry-leaves/#wprm-recipe-53349-step-0-4",
